---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { pathways } from '../../data/catalogue.mjs';
---
<Layout title="The reading room" active="Reading room" description="Three guided routes through the second-edition chapters, with original companion connections, discussion questions, and civilian exercises.">
  <div class="wrap page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Companion notes · Teaching & discussion</p><h1>Bring a question<br /><em>to the book.</em></h1><p class="lead">A few routes through the chapter topics, with questions to carry into the reading. Start with the problem you want to understand, then return to the authors for the substance.</p></div>
  <div class="wrap reading-room-grid"><div><p class="editorial-label">Original companion material</p><div class="prose"><p>These reading notes suggest connections between chapter topics. Each sequence connects the scope of particular contributions while keeping their different purposes visible. The notes supplement the chapters rather than replace their arguments. Each note identifies its proposed sequence and offers an original discussion exercise. The chapter pages keep the authorship and edition of each contribution visible, so a reading sequence does not turn several distinct contributions into one anonymous account.</p><p>For teaching, ask readers to make a short record of the decision, evidence, assumptions, and remaining uncertainty in each contribution they study. Compare those records before trying to combine the methods. A disagreement about objectives is different from a disagreement about an estimate, and neither becomes clearer by putting both under the heading of uncertainty. The notes below offer several places to begin that conversation.</p></div></div><div class="reading-notes">{pathways.map((p, i) => <article><p class="eyebrow">Reading note 0{i + 1} · {p.numbers.length} chapters</p><h2><a href={`/reading-room/${p.slug}/`}>{p.title}</a></h2><p>{p.label}</p><a class="text-link" href={`/reading-room/${p.slug}/`}>Open the reading note <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>)}</div></div>
  <aside class="wrap source-note reading-boundary"><h2>Using the companion</h2><p>Chapter records link to the book and its published contents. Read the full contributions in the handbook, then use these original questions and exercises for discussion. The print view includes the note’s title, edition, and web address.</p></aside>
</Layout>
